least vertex of a symmetric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"difference. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count once. The cost is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s: O(m √n) on bipartite components.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"minimumVertexCover()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"König’s minimum vertex cover of a bipartite graph (NetworkX "},{"code":"to_vertex_cover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cover): from a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp on the sides), Z is the set of vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached from the free left vertices by alternating paths, an edge not in the matching from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most left vertices, so it does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depend on the matching. O(m √n)."}],"role":"symbol","title":"minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyw